5406"} "Zhang Xiangsen"] " (1995), Turkey’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/56868"} "Halil Mutlu"] " (1994), and Bulgaria’s " [:a {:href ""} "Ivan Ivanov"] " (1993). Mutlu took the lead with a world record snatch of 132.5 kg, and maintained it with an Olympic record 155.0 kg in the clean &amp; jerk to win the gold medal over Zhang. The bronze went to Bulgarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/55306"} "Sevdalin Minchev"] ", who had the second best clean &amp; jerk with 152.5 kg, as Ivanov struggled in the snatch, lifting only 112.5 kg, and finished sixth."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Mutlu was a native Bulgarian, born Huben Hubenov. Like his idol, " [:a {:href "/athletes/56874"} "Naim Süleymanoğlu"] ", Mutlu was in the Muslim minority in Bulgaria, so he emigrated to Turkey to compete for that nation. He would win gold medals again in 2000 and 2004 as a bantamweight."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Kilograms"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/56868"} "Halil Mutlu"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/TUR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/TUR.png"}] "TUR"]] [:td {} "287.5"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/55406"} "Zhang Xiangsen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "280.0"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/55306"} "Sevdalin Minchev"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BUL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: mid